License  : MIT, Copyright (c) 2023 Unstoppable Games, Inc. (see LICENSE)

Why vendored: neither the git dependency nor the scarbs.xyz release (1.3.1) compiles with Cairo
2.19.4. The only blocker is test code: `assert(a <= b == false, ..)` is now a PARSER error
(E1028 "Consecutive comparison operators are not allowed"), and parser errors are reported even
inside `#[cfg(test)]` modules of a dependency.

Local changes:
  - src/f64/math/ops.cairo, src/f128/math/ops.cairo: 36 test assertions rewritten from
    `assert(x OP y == false, ..)` to `assert((x OP y) == false, ..)`. No non-test line is touched.
  - Removed: src/math/, src/types/ (dead duplicates, not declared in lib.cairo), *.js helpers,
    test/ directory, JS packaging files.
  - Scarb.toml rewritten (name/version/edition kept: cubit 1.4.0, edition 2023_10).
